' plan-115-A guardrail: the entry rule NARROWED to ISOLATED, it did not vanish.
'
' The sibling fixture thread-start-local-entry-valid proves a bare local
' ISOLATED FUNC is now a valid entry. This one proves that accepting a bare name
' did not accept EVERY bare name: a local FUNC with the right shape but no
' ISOLATED marker is still rejected. Without this, deleting the entry rule
' outright would look green.
IMPORT thread

' Correct signature for an entry in every respect EXCEPT the ISOLATED marker.
FUNC plainWorker(t AS ThreadWorker OF Nothing TO Integer, seed AS Integer) AS Integer
  RETURN seed + 1
END FUNC

FUNC main AS Integer
  LET a AS Thread OF Nothing TO Integer = thread::start(plainWorker, 10)
  RETURN thread::waitFor(a)
END FUNC
